= BITwiki Ontology Expansion =

== Overview ==

This directory contains the '''expanded ontology specifications''' for BITwiki, extending the core knowledge graph with 12 composable entity types, 12 relationship patterns, and comprehensive epistemic frameworks.

== Deliverables ==

=== 1. Expanded Entity Types ===
'''File:''' `BITwiki_Expanded_Entity_Types.wiki`

Extended specifications for 12 composable entity types:

| Entity Type | Description | Page Type |
|-------------|-------------|-----------|
| '''Concept''' | Abstract ideas, categories, mental constructs | Topic |
| '''Process''' | Dynamic sequences, workflows, transformations | Topic |
| '''System''' | Organized collections of interacting components | Topic |
| '''Entity''' | Distinct objects or beings | Topic |
| '''Agent''' | Entities capable of action/decision | Agent |
| '''Artifact''' | Created objects that carry knowledge | Dataset |
| '''Relationship''' | Connections between entities | Topic |
| '''Event''' | Temporal occurrences with significance | Topic |
| '''State''' | Conditions at a point in time | Topic |
| '''Data''' | Structured information | Dataset |
| '''Knowledge''' | Justified true beliefs or validated information | Topic |
| '''Model''' | Simplified representations of phenomena | Topic |

=== 2. Relationship Pattern Catalog ===
'''File:''' `BITwiki_Relationship_Pattern_Catalog.wiki`

Twelve core relationship patterns with SMW implementation:

| Pattern | Domain → Range | Cardinality | Transitive |
|---------|----------------|-------------|------------|
| '''Depends On''' | Any → Any | many-to-many | Yes |
| '''Implements''' | Impl/Proc → Concept | many-to-many | No |
| '''Uses''' | Agent/Proc → Tool/Res | many-to-many | No |
| '''Creates''' | Agent → Artifact | one-to-many | No |
| '''Influences''' | Any → Any | many-to-many | Yes |
| '''Part Of''' | Any → Any | many-to-many | Yes |
| '''Precedes''' | Event/Proc → Event/Proc | many-to-many | Yes |
| '''References''' | Any → Resource | many-to-many | No |
| '''Supports''' | Data → Knowledge | many-to-many | No |
| '''Contradicts''' | Data/Claim → Claim | many-to-many | No |
| '''Extends''' | Any → Any | many-to-many | Yes |
| '''Governs''' | Agent/Org → Proc/Prot | many-to-many | No |

=== 3. Ontology Alignment Matrix ===
'''File:''' `BITwiki_Ontology_Alignment_Matrix.wiki`

Cross-domain synthesis mapping to major ontologies:
* '''Schema.org''' → Web standards alignment
* '''FOAF''' → Agent and social relationships
* '''Dublin Core''' → Metadata properties
* '''SKOS''' → Concept and taxonomy mapping
* '''Wikidata''' → Entity and property alignment
* '''BIBO''' → Bibliographic resources
* '''PROV-O''' → Provenance and attribution

=== 4. Epistemic Status Taxonomy ===
'''File:''' `BITwiki_Epistemic_Status_Taxonomy.wiki`

Six epistemic descriptors replacing numeric confidence scores:

| Status | Meaning | Use Case |
|--------|---------|----------|
| '''Established''' | Widely validated, consensus | Foundational knowledge |
| '''Developing''' | Active validation ongoing | Emerging research |
| '''Preliminary''' | Initial evidence, needs review | Early findings |
| '''Speculative''' | Hypothesis, limited evidence | Theoretical work |
| '''Disputed''' | Active controversy | Contested claims |
| '''Deprecated''' | Superseded or obsolete | Historical reference |

Includes status transition workflows and claim-level epistemic tracking.

=== 5. Visual Diagram Specification ===
'''File:''' `BITwiki_Visual_Diagram_Specification.wiki`

Six diagram types in Mermaid and DOT formats:

# '''Entity Type Hierarchy''' - 12-type taxonomy
# '''Core Relationship Patterns''' - 12-pattern network graph
# '''Epistemic Status Flow''' - State machine transitions
# '''Domain Alignment Network''' - Cross-domain mappings
# '''Query Pattern Visualization''' - NL to SMW pipeline
# '''EPV Framework''' - Event-Process-Value model

All diagrams use valid Mermaid syntax with:
* Underscores for entity names (MY_ENTITY)
* Quoted multi-word labels ("depends on")
* Proper cardinality notation

== SMW Compatibility ==

All specifications align with existing BITwiki SMW infrastructure:
* ✅ Property types: Page, Text, Number, Date, URL, Boolean
* ✅ Category syntax: `[[Category:...]]`
* ✅ Property declarations: `[[Has type::...]]`
* ✅ Query syntax: `{{#ask:...}}`
* ✅ Subobjects: `{{#subobject:...}}`
* ✅ Inverse properties: `[[Has inverse property::...]]`

